    "narrative": "As we navigate the final stretch of the season, our offensive output hinges on today\u2019s matchup against Robert Gasser. **Kyle Tucker** headlines our lineup with a 67.66 score, serving as our primary engine today. While his matchup against a left-handed arm usually triggers a platoon discount, **Kyle Tucker**\u2019s elite base skill and solidified #4 spot in the order keep his floor exceptionally high. We are also deploying **Andy Pages** in the UTIL slot with a 56.47 score. Though his position at #7 in the order caps his RBI potential, **Andy Pages** benefits from Gasser\u2019s deliberate pace and high-latency delivery, which historically opens up higher success rates for stolen bases\u2014a critical factor given our aggressive pursuit of the category.\n\nThe decision-making process today was dictated largely by the league schedule, as several of our heavy hitters are inactive. Both **Gunnar Henderson** and **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** are sidelined due to team off-days, while **Luis Robert Jr.** remains held out on the IL, frustrating our ability to stack elite speed. **Jackson Merrill** also sits today, leaving us with a thinner than ideal roster. Among those on the active bench, no player managed to eclipse the 50-point threshold, confirming the decision to roll with **Kyle Tucker** and **Andy Pages** as the sole representatives for the Austin Waves. We remain cautious regarding the \"Lineup Pending\" status for both, as any shift down the order for **Andy Pages** could further compress his daily efficiency score below our preferred 60-point start threshold.",
